Synchronization Issue
---------------------------
- When there is time mapping issue between tool and application then Selenium
give us Synchronization issue


Static wait we can add using JAVA
-------------------
Thread.sleep(2000);

Selenium Support Dynamic Waits
----------------------------
1.Implicit Wait
-----------------------------
- Implicit wait is Global wait applicable for all the elements in Script
- Implicit wait default timeout  is 0sec
- Implicit wait suppose I used as 10sec and element needed on 6sec so remaining 4sec selenium 
will not wait ,it will continue with next element
- Add Implicit wait after driver session

Syntax
-----------
driver.manage().timeouts().implicitlyWait(Duration.ofSeconds(10));

2.Explicit Wait
--------------------------
-Explicit wiat is applicable for single webelement
- we can apply wait on element based on conditions
-Explicit wait implemented in Selenium using two classes
1.WebDriverWait class
2.FluentWait Class

WebDriverWait(C) extends FluentWait(C) implements Wait(I)

