By xpath
=================
- Xpath is path of the element from Html and Xml document
- Xpath identify element directly from DOM (Document object model)
- Xpath can travel in both direction (parent to child and viceversa)
- Xpath support methods
- Xpath support axies

------Html Dom------------------
<html>----------Root element
<head>
</head>

<body>
<input>
<a>-----------------webelement
<button>
<div>
</body>
</html>
------------------------------------
Types of Xpath
===================
1.Absolute Xpath(Full xpath)
-----------------------------
- Absolute xpath identify element from root element
- Absolute xpath starts with '/'

/html/body/div[2]/div/div/div/div[2]/div/form/div[1]/input

2.Relative Xpath (partial xpath)
---------------------------------------
- Relative xpath identify element based on relative property
- Relative xpath starts with '//'

//*[@id="input-email"]

here * means any tagname 
Identify element where tagname could be any and id should be input-email

=================================================
Syntax
================
//tagname[@attribute='value']


=========================================
Xpath with Operators
============================
1.and  (&&)
------------------------
Syntax
-----------
//tagname[@attribute1='value' and @attribute2='value']

2.or  (||)
----------------------
Syntax
-----------
//tagname[@attribute1='value' or @attribute2='value']

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Xpath With indexing
=======================

Syntax
-------------
(xpath)[index]

OR
(xpath)[position()=index]

==================================================
Xpath Methods
====================
1. text(): 
--------------------
text() identify element based on visible text 
this method never ignore white space and because of this text() will fail if element text is 
available with white space

Syntax
--------------
//tagname[text()='visible text']

-------------------------------------------
2.narmalize-space()
----------------------------
normalize-space() identify element based on visible text 
this method ignore white space (It act like trim()from String) 


Syntax
--------------
//tagname[normalize-space()='visible text']
--------------------------------------------------
3.contains(): partial match
---------------------
Syntax
----------------

//tagname[contains(@attribute,'partial value')]

Or

//tagname[contains(text(),'partial text')]
Or

//tagname[contains(normalize-space(),'partial text')]


4.starts-with(): prefix value
-------------------------------------
//tagname[starts-with(@attribute,'prefix value')]

Or

//tagname[starts-with(text(),'prefix text')]
Or

//tagname[starts-with(normalize-space(),'prefix text')]

